 "text": "Road and Bridge - McKenzie County, ND\nYou are using an outdated browser. Please upgrade your browser to improve your experience.\nSkip to content\nSkip to navigation\nSite map\nOfficial government website\nQuick top menu links Jobs\nEvents\nAction toolbar\nAnswers\nPayments\nReport Issue\nTranslate\nTranslate language select\nSelect language Afrikaans Albanian Amharic Arabic Armenian Azerbaijani Basque Belarusian Bengali Bosnian Bulgarian Catalan Cebuano Chichewa Chinese (Simplified) Chinese (Traditional) Corsican Croatian Czech Danish Dutch English Esperanto Estonian Filipino Finnish French Frisian Galician Georgian German Greek Gujarati Haitian Creole Hausa Hawaiian Hebrew Hindi Hmong Hungarian Icelandic Igbo Indonesian Irish Italian Japanese Javanese Kannada Kazakh Khmer Korean Kurdish (Kurmanji) Kyrgyz Lao Latin Latvian Lithuanian Luxembourgish Macedonian Malagasy Malay Malayalam Maltese Maori Marathi Mongolian Myanmar (Burmese) Nepali Norwegian Pashto Persian Polish Portuguese Punjabi Romanian Russian Samoan Scottish Gaelic Serbian Sesotho Shona Sindhi Sinhala Slovak Slovenian Somali Spanish Sundanese Swahili Swedish Tajik Tamil Telugu Thai Turkish Ukrainian Urdu Uzbek Vietnamese Welsh Xhosa Yiddish Yoruba Zulu\nSearch\nMcKenzie County, ND\nMenu\nPrimary menu links\nCommunity\nDepartments\nBoards\nServices\nNews\nContact\nMcKenzie County, ND\nRoad and Bridge\nPolicies and Standards\nPermits\nAgreements\nRoad Restrictions\nCapital Improvement Plan\nProject Information\nPublic Works Subcommittee\nBack\nDesign Standards and Typical Section\nContact\nRoad and Bridge Department\n(701) 444-2600\n(701) 444-4113 (FAX)\nsforeman@co.mckenzie.nd.us\nMcKenzie County Public Works Building\n1300 12th St SE Ste. 240\nWatford City, ND 58854\nImage by: Micheala Dorman\nAbout\nThe McKenzie County Road and Bridge Department is responsible for maintaining, repairing, and constructing County roads and bridges. The Road and Bridge Department also provides support to organized townships to assist with maintaining and repairing Township roads. The Road and Bridge Department works holistically to prioritize road and bridge maintenance and improvement needs through the capital improvement planning process. The Engineering Department is housed within the Road and Bridge Department and permits encumbrances within the right of way including utilities and approaches. The Road and Bridge Department also issues overweight/oversized truck permits on County and Township roads via LoadPass Permits.\nRoad Updates\nFor updates on road closures, incidents, construction and weather conditions, click the link below.\nNDDOT Travel Map\nMcKenzie County Road Information\nRoad and Bridge Staff\nName | Position | | Phone | Contact | |\nGrace Demars |\nEngineering Director |\n|\n701-444-7141 |\ngdemars@co.mckenzie.nd.us |\n|\nLayton Northrop |\nRoad and Bridge Superintendent |\n|\n701-444-7178 |\nlnorthrop@co.mckenzie.nd.us |\n|\nTim Pickering |\nPermitting Specialist |\n|\n701-444-7150 |\ntpickering@co.mckenzie.nd.us |\n|\nCindy Glover |\nRoad and Bridge Project Specialist |\n|\n701-444-7143 |\ncglover@co.mckenzie.nd.us |\n|\nCassie Cullinan |\nRoad and Bridge Specialist |\n|\n701-444-7177 |\ncassiec@co.mckenzie.nd.us |\n|\nSamantha Foreman |\nRoad and Bridge Specialist |\n|\n701-444-7178 |\nsforeman@co.mckenzie.nd.us |\n|\nHelpful\n-->\nShare\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\n-->\nSize\n+\nReset\na\n−\nWelcome\nAbout\nCommunity\nNews\nEvents\nJobs\nEngage\nConnect\nFeedback\nHelp\nServices\nContact\nDirectory\nSitemap\nPowered by\n1 --> Get answers\nMy services\nMake a payment\nReport an issue\n1 -->\nSelect question type\nCorrectional Facility\nProperty and Housing\nBuilding Codes and Zoning\nJobs\nGeneral Government\nClose window\nSearch Site\nSearch\nClose window",
